§§ `67(b) — choosing between two insured parents`

-- The child's own parent: natural, or adoptive (fork F8: an adopter is the child's parent in
-- every respect, and is read into the first limb, not the second).
@ref National Insurance Law s 67(b) (source line 818); s 1 "ילד" (source line 170)
GIVEN `the entry` IS A `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the child's own parent:` `the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entry`'s `standing`
    WHEN `the child's natural parent`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the child's adoptive parent` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                              FALSE

@ref National Insurance Law s 67(b) (source line 818): "הורה טבעי"
GIVEN `the entry` IS A `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a natural parent:` `the entry` MEANS
    `the entry`'s `standing` EQUALS `the child's natural parent`

@ref National Insurance Law s 67(b) (source line 818)
GIVEN `the entry` IS A `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the father:` `the entry` MEANS
    `the entry`'s `father or mother` EQUALS `the child's father`

-- First limb: "a child who has two parents shall be counted with the insured father unless
-- he is with the mother only". "With the mother only": with her and not with the father
-- (fork F12).
-- src:818 | (ב) ילד שיש לו שני הורים, יבוא במנין האב המבוטח זולת אם הוא נמצא עם האם בלבד; ילד שיש לו הורה טבעי והורה אחר והם מבוטחים, יבוא במנין ילדי אותו הורה אשר עמו הוא נמצא.
@ref National Insurance Law s 67(b), first limb (source line 818)
GIVEN `the father`  IS A `A parent in a child's record`
      `the mother`  IS A `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 67(b), first limb — between the father` `the father` `and the mother` `the mother` MEANS
    IF       "זולת אם הוא נמצא עם האם בלבד" ...     `the mother`'s `the child is with this person`
                                            AND NOT `the father`'s `the child is with this person`
    THEN `the mother`'s `name of the person`
    ELSE `the father`'s `name of the person`

-- Second limb: "a child who has a natural parent and another parent and they are insured
-- shall be counted among the children of that parent with whom he is".
@ref National Insurance Law s 67(b), second limb (source line 818)
GIVEN `the natural parent` IS A `A parent in a child's record`
      `the other parent`   IS A `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 67(b), second limb — between the natural parent` `the natural parent` `and the other parent` `the other parent` MEANS
    BRANCH IF     `the natural parent`'s `the child is with this person`
              AND NOT `the other parent`'s `the child is with this person`
           THEN   `the natural parent`'s `name of the person`
           IF     `the other parent`'s `the child is with this person`
              AND NOT `the natural parent`'s `the child is with this person`
           THEN   `the other parent`'s `name of the person`
           OTHERWISE `section 67(b) does not say in whose count a child is counted who has a natural parent and another insured parent and is with both of them, or with neither`

@ref National Insurance Law s 67(b) (source line 818)
GIVEN `the one`   IS A `A parent in a child's record`
      `the other` IS A `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 67(b) — the insured parent in whose count the child is, between` `the one` `and` `the other` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the child's own parent:` `the one` AND `the child's own parent:` `the other`
           THEN BRANCH IF `the father:` `the one` AND NOT `the father:` `the other`
                       THEN `s 67(b), first limb — between the father` `the one` `and the mother` `the other`
                       IF `the father:` `the other` AND NOT `the father:` `the one`
                       THEN `s 67(b), first limb — between the father` `the other` `and the mother` `the one`
                       OTHERWISE `section 67(b) does not say in whose count a child is counted whose two insured parents are both its fathers or both its mothers`
           IF `a natural parent:` `the one` AND NOT `the child's own parent:` `the other`
           THEN `s 67(b), second limb — between the natural parent` `the one` `and the other parent` `the other`
           IF `a natural parent:` `the other` AND NOT `the child's own parent:` `the one`
           THEN `s 67(b), second limb — between the natural parent` `the other` `and the other parent` `the one`
           OTHERWISE `section 67(b) does not say in whose count a child is counted whose two insured parents are neither the child's own two parents nor a natural parent and another parent`

§§ `Section 67 — the parent in whose count a child is`

-- s 69A reaches the child when one of its insured parents is a man (its father, for this
-- Chapter) with children by more than one woman.
@ref National Insurance Law s 69A (source line 843)
GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family on a day`, `the child`  IS A `A child`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 69A may apply, in` `the family` `, to the count of` `the child` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` MEANS
    any (GIVEN e YIELD     `the father:` e
                       AND any (GIVEN p YIELD p's `children by more than one woman`)
                               (`the persons named` (e's `name of the person`) `in` `the family`))
        (`the insured parents of` `the child` `in` `the family` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading`)

-- The choice among the insured parents, before s 71 is consulted.
@ref National Insurance Law s 67(b) (source line 818)
GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family on a day`, `the child`  IS A `A child`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 67 — the insured parent chosen, in` `the family` `, for` `the child` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the number of candidates` EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING
           IF `the number of candidates` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST ((at `the candidates` 0)'s `name of the person`)
           IF `the number of candidates` EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (`s 67(b) — the insured parent in whose count the child is, between` (at `the candidates` 0) `and` (at `the candidates` 1))
           OTHERWISE `section 67(b) does not say in whose count a child with more than two insured parents is counted`
    WHERE
        `the candidates`           MEANS `the insured parents of` `the child` `in` `the family` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading`
        `the number of candidates` MEANS count `the candidates`

-- s 71 reaches the child when a parent who was insured has died or ceased to be insured and
-- the child is not in the count of an insured parent entitled to the allowance: then s 71,
-- not this row, says what is paid. Where the chosen parent is entitled, s 71's own proviso
-- ("if the child had a second parent and he is entitled") points to the same parent.
@ref National Insurance Law s 71 (source line 851)
GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family on a day`, `the child`  IS A `A child`
      `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 71 may apply, in` `the family` `, to` `the child` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` MEANS
        NOT null (`the parents of` `the child` `who were insured, in` `the family` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading`)
    AND NOT `chosen and entitled`
    WHERE
        `chosen and entitled` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 67 — the insured parent chosen, in` `the family` `, for` `the child` `, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading`
            WHEN NOTHING          THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST `the name` THEN any (GIVEN p YIELD `s 66 — entitled to a monthly child allowance for each child in the count, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` p)
                                          (`the persons named` `the name` `in` `the family`)

-- The section's answer: the parent in whose count the child is, or NOTHING. Asked of the day, or
-- (0.2.0) of the month s 72 pays; the day's form is at the end. A day before 1 May 2015 is declined
-- first (nii-il06-period.l4); any day of a month answers alike, as the text took effect on a 1st.
@ref National Insurance Law s 67 (source lines 816-818), s 65 (source lines 799-809)
GIVEN `the question` IS A `The question asked of a family on a day`, `the readings` IS A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`
      `the family` IS A `A family on a day`, `the child`  IS A `A child`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 67 — the insured parent in whose count, asked` `the question` `, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `, is` `the child` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the deposited text of sections 65 to 68 was in force on` (`the family`'s `the day`)
           THEN `this model answers days from 1 May 2015, when sections 1 and 68 took their present wording; the text in force before then is not in its sources`
           IF NOT `s 65 — a child for this Chapter, asked` `the question` `, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `:` `the child`
           THEN NOTHING
           IF `section 69A may apply, in` `the family` `, to the count of` `the child` `, reading a resident housewife as` (`the readings`'s `for a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`)
           THEN `section 69A, for an insured man with children by more than one woman, displaces sections 67 and 68 and is not encoded in this model`
           IF `section 71 may apply, in` `the family` `, to` `the child` `, reading a resident housewife as` (`the readings`'s `for a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`)
           THEN `section 71, on the allowance paid by virtue of a parent who died or ceased to be insured, is not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE `s 67 — the insured parent chosen, in` `the family` `, for` `the child` `, reading a resident housewife as` (`the readings`'s `for a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`)

§§ `67(a) — one count only`

-- src:817 | (א) לא יבוא ילד, בפרק זמן אחד, במנין ילדים של יותר מהורה מבוטח אחד.
-- Held by construction: the section's answer names at most one parent per child, and names
-- are unique once the facts are checked. Stated as a rule so that it can be asserted, and so
-- that the family-level answer can consult it, which forces every child's count to be
-- settled (and any refusal above to reach the caller) before an answer is returned
-- (phrasebook 11.8).
@ref National Insurance Law s 67(a) (source line 817)
GIVEN `the question` IS A `The question asked of a family on a day`, `the readings` IS A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`, `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 67(a) — no child is counted with more than one insured parent, asked` `the question` `, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` MEANS
    all (GIVEN c YIELD count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD `s 67 — the insured parent in whose count, asked` `the question` `, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `, is` c EQUALS JUST (p's `name`))
                                     (`the family`'s `the persons`))
                       AT MOST 1)
        (`the family`'s `the children`)

§§ `The count, in order`

@ref National Insurance Law s 67 (source lines 816-818); the order of the count is fork F4
GIVEN `the question` IS A `The question asked of a family on a day`
      `the readings` IS A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`
      `the family`   IS A `A family on a day`
      `the person`   IS A `A person`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A child`
`s 67 — the count of children, asked` `the question` `, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `, of` `the person` MEANS
    sortBy (GIVEN x, y YIELD x's `date of birth` AT MOST y's `date of birth`)
           (filter (GIVEN c YIELD `s 67 — the insured parent in whose count, asked` `the question` `, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `, is` c EQUALS JUST (`the person`'s `name`))
                   (`the family`'s `the children`))

§§ `The day's forms, and the month's (versions 0.2.0 and 0.3.0)`

-- Each rule above is asked of a question (nii-il06-nouns.l4, `The question asked of a family on a
-- day`) and, from version 0.3.0, at the readings of forks F18 and F2 (`The readings this model
-- takes where the text does not decide`; nii-s65-interpretation.l4). The forms by the names of
-- version 0.1.0 answer the day at the readings the switches name; the forms with `, reading` take
-- the readings the caller names. Where a reading is the declined one, each answers what the two
-- other readings both answer and is declined where they differ (`the answer to`, in
-- nii-s65-interpretation.l4). The month's take `A family in a month`, whose children are the
-- ones s 72 pays for in the month; a child paid for in the month of its 18th birthday, or of a
-- birth by the 15th, is in the count at its place by date of birth (fork F19). The lines cited
-- elsewhere (169, 223-227) hold the rules they held before 0.2.0.

@ref National Insurance Law s 67 (source lines 816-818), s 65 (source lines 799-809)
GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings this model takes where the text does not decide`
      `the family`   IS A `A family on a day`
      `the child`    IS A `A child`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 67 — the insured parent in whose count, reading` `the readings` `, in` `the family` `, is` `the child` MEANS
    `the answer to` (GIVEN r YIELD `s 67 — the insured parent in whose count, asked` `the allowance on the family's day` `, reading` r `, in` `the family` `, is` `the child`)
        `at` `the readings` `, fork F18 mattering:` (`fork F18 can matter in` `the family`) `, fork F2 mattering:` (`fork F2 can matter for` `the child`)
        `, two answers merged by` (GIVEN x, y YIELD IF x EQUALS y THEN JUST x ELSE NOTHING)

